// fixture-242: MAN-DEP-NAME-INVALID — dep name with trailing newline.
//
// A KDL quoted string node name whose last character is a newline escape (\n)
// MUST be rejected with MAN-DEP-NAME-INVALID.
//
// Python's `re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_\-]+$")` incorrectly accepts a trailing
// newline because `$` matches before a trailing \n in Python's regex engine.
// Rust's `valid_flag_name` (byte-by-byte check) correctly rejects it.
//
// Without this fix, a dep named "validname\n" passes Python's guard and
// reaches nim.cfg `--path:` / `-d:` emission, injecting an extra newline and
// potentially arbitrary subsequent nim.cfg directives if the name contains
// additional content after the newline.
//
// Fix: use `_FLAG_NAME_CHARSET_RE.fullmatch(s)` (or `\Z` anchor) so the
// trailing newline is NOT silently swallowed by `$`.
//
// Cross-impl divergence: RED in Python before fix, GREEN after fix;
// already GREEN in Rust (valid_flag_name checks every byte).
name "pkg"
deps {
    "validname\n" git=(url)"https://github.com/example/foo" ref="main"
}
